    "done_when": "scripts/nova_lane/run.sh (generalising scripts/h200_test_lane/run.sh, which keeps working as a thin caller) takes a script or pytest target, a rung preference (h200 then titan then cpu by default), cores, memory and an absolute log path. It applies the rules in AGENTS.md 'Compute hierarchy' and 'An exact sync strips the extras': H200 via --partition=betelgeuse --reservation=gpu_0003_grpA --gres=gpu:1; titan via --partition=titan --gres=gpu:1; CPU via --partition=all_debug with JAX_PLATFORMS=cpu; an explicit --mem, refusing --mem=0; TMPDIR=/tmp exported at submit and in the payload; unset UV_NO_SYNC UV_RUN_RECURSION_DEPTH; no uv on the compute node (the shared interpreter /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/nova/.venv/bin/python with PYTHONPATH); a real submission, never a --test-only decision; falls to the next rung only when squeue shows a real submission still PENDING with a resources or configuration reason after a bounded wait. The log header records the rung used, the job id and the git revision. Evidence under docs/figures/forward-solver-route-integrity/lane-launcher/ (logs force-added): (1) bash -n and shellcheck clean if shellcheck exists; (2) a --dry-run mode prints the sbatch line for each rung and refuses --mem=0, shown in a log; (3) one real CPU-rung run of a 5-second python -c target writes its header and exit status; (4) tests/test_nova_lane_launcher.py asserts the dry-run lines and the --mem=0 refusal (negative control: allowing --mem=0 makes it fail, logged).",
